# Public repository safety

- Read and follow `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` before editing or publishing.
- Never commit secrets, setup bundles, environment files, local databases/logs,
  internal URLs, employee/customer data, private project details or proprietary code.
- This applies to tests, examples, images, commit messages and PR descriptions too.
- Use synthetic examples (`alex@example.com`, `gitlab.example.com`); read real
  deployment values from local settings, not hardcoded defaults.
- Stage explicit paths; inspect staged content and run the public-tree check
  and redacted staged Gitleaks scan before committing, plus history scan before push.
- Do not bypass findings, force-add private files, or print credentials in output.
- If sensitivity is uncertain, stop and ask. If exposed, notify the maintainer
  privately and rotate credentials; do not rewrite shared history without approval.
